  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 131 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nWe welcome the ridge back overhead during the day on Sunday as a \nbroad jet streak moves across the northern part of the country. This \nwill be accompanied by a weak frontal boundary attempting to move \ninto the northern part of the CWA. Those two competing factors will \nactually produce a weak gradient in high temperatures by Monday \nafternoon with hotter temperatures clustered around the Red River \nand highs in northern Oklahoma potentially remaining in the 90s. \nThat frontal boundary is also the best chance anyone in our area has \nto receive significant drought-busting rainfall. Even those odds are \nnot all that good, and mostly limited to far northern Oklahoma.\n\nGuidance is starting to indicate that a trough could dig southward \nto near or into our CWA by the middle of next week. It's unclear \nwhether this scenario comes to pass or not, but bears watching in \nthe coming days. If we did get a trough passage, there would likely \nbe impactful weather of some sort for mid-to-late next week - \nperhaps more extreme heat, or fire weather, or maybe even \nrain/storms.\n\nMeister",
